/**
 * @file sha2
 * @author jung-kwang lee (ntoskrnl7@gmail.com)
 * @brief The SHA-2 family from FIPS 180-4
 *
 * SHA-224 and SHA-256 share the 32 bit compression function. SHA-384,
 * SHA-512, SHA-512/224 and SHA-512/256 share the 64 bit one. The public
 * types below keep those two engines in one place while giving each variant
 * its own initial value and digest length.
 *
 * Input is supplied as byte strings, so the FIPS bit-string algorithms are
 * implemented for messages whose length is a multiple of eight. A context is
 * consumed by finish. It can be reset explicitly, but cannot be copied or
 * used after a move or finish without that reset.
 *
 * @version 0.1
 *
 * @copyright Copyright (c) 2022 C++ Cryptographics template library Authors
 */
